# Line-ending normalization. Text files are auto-detected and stored as LF in
# history, so a Windows checkout does not show the whole tree as modified (there
# is otherwise no policy, and the SV/generated files are LF).
#
# Deliberately NOT `eol=lf`: the generator writes the host's NATIVE newline
# (Python emits CRLF on Windows), and the byte-identity gate compares the
# checked-out gen/ against a fresh render — forcing an LF checkout while the
# generator emits CRLF would make them mismatch on Windows. `text=auto` keeps
# the history LF and the diff clean without dictating the working-tree EOL.
* text=auto
